cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Adyghe AI language test — protocol, frozen instrument, raw data and analysis tool"
message: >-
  If you use this instrument, its data or its analysis tool, please cite
  this repository. Cite a tagged release, not the main branch.
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: "Nemlioğlu"
    given-names: "Mehmet Uğur"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1969-2356"
  - family-names: "Abregova Nemlioğlu"
    given-names: "Saida"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-2467-6692"
repository-code: "https://github.com/nemerko/ady-kbd-ai-language-test"
url: "https://github.com/nemerko/ady-kbd-ai-language-test"
abstract: >-
  A small, versioned instrument for measuring whether widely used AI chat
  tools, in their free tiers, can process Adyghe (ady) input and produce
  semantically adequate Adyghe output, together with the raw answers it
  produced, the marking workbooks labelled by two evaluators by consensus,
  the tables derived from them, and the C# tool that performs the
  character-level analysis (palochka use, Latin look-alikes, mixed scripts,
  normalisation form).
keywords:
  - Adyghe
  - Circassian
  - low-resource languages
  - language technology evaluation
  - digital language planning
  - large language models
  - palochka
  - Unicode
